Modifications made in ProkBot Plus (2026-11-07 to 2026-11-18)
--------------------------------------------------------------

1. Windows x64 client (new)
   - On 2026-11-16, the Windows patcher moved to the official Windows 1.1.0
     input. windows/tools/desktop-recipes/ (generator, anchored edit list and
     the project code appended to original modules) produces the recipes from
     the user's own installer. mac/clients/desktop/ adds the 1.1.0 interfaces:
     per-edge RPC registration and window visibility events (main.mjs,
     local-services.mjs), dictation through the Host (dictation.mjs), search
     mapping (gateway.mjs) and startup defaults. The 0.71.2 Windows inputs
     moved to windows/patchers/desktop/0.71.2/ for the Android client, and the
     earlier 1.1.0 research replays under windows/tools/compat/ were removed.
   - In 1.3.0, 0.71.2 became the Windows fallback: inputs.mjs lists the
     recommended release and the fallbacks and recognizes an input by size
     and SHA-256, patch.mjs gained --version, and known-unsupported.json was
     removed.
   - On 2026-11-14, added explicit incompatible-input diagnostics, corrected
     desktop/Android connection lifecycle handling and preserved desktop
     settings on save failures. No official code is included.
   - The temporary uninstaller releases the installation working directory;
     a disposable native CLI regression covers the legacy side-by-side path.
   - windows/: patcher, Windows recipes (1.1.0 generated by
     windows/tools/desktop-recipes/, 0.71.2 ported from the macOS recipes),
     per-user installer source, prebuilt grokbot-tailcat.exe and installer
     stub, tests.
   - mac/clients/desktop/: cross-platform changes shared by the macOS and
     Windows clients (platform.mjs, main.mjs, connection.mjs, settings.mjs,
     sounds.mjs, connect.css, native-provider.mjs, codex-bridge.mjs,
     codex-process.mjs). Windows command output uses the original daemon's
     UTF-8 console option (local-exec.mjs). Host image paths are parsed with
     POSIX rules on Windows (attachments.mjs).
   - host/runtime/host-computers.mjs, native-desktop.mjs, codex-prompt.mjs,
     host/server/desktop-capabilities.mjs: the Host recognizes Windows
     computers.

   - mac/clients/desktop/workspace.css and workspace-keys.cjs: wide reply
     tables, dialog send shortcuts and empty catalog-search dismissal, shared
     by both desktop clients and the unofficial Android renderer.

2. Model API formats
   - New Anthropic Messages and OpenAI Responses adapters next to OpenAI Chat:
     host/runtime/anthropic-messages.mjs, openai-responses.mjs,
     openai-chat.mjs, model-common.mjs (new); model-session.mjs,
     model-policy.mjs, model-router.mjs, model-errors.mjs,
     model-observation.mjs, config.mjs, host/server/models.mjs, index.mjs,
     public/model.js, public/locales-en.js and public/ids.js (changed or new).
   - "minimal" reasoning effort, reasoning provenance tags, optional-parameter
     fallback, connection test and auto review for all three formats.
   - Provider/model/format-scoped reasoning replay, ordered primary/backup
     routing with upstream-I/O idle deadlines and explicit quota exhaustion
     classification, incremental large-event SSE parsing and restartable client
     stream subscriptions. A backup sharing a key is skipped only when the
     provider explicitly reports quota exhaustion; ordinary 503, timeout and
     network failures may still try that backup.
   - Per-Bot model routes and profiles (host/runtime/model-routing.mjs, contributed
     through pull request #2), the
     rewritten model page, guarded manual summarization (host-summarize.mjs),
     threshold compaction, and rejection of malformed provider function names
     (model-rejection-guard.mjs). The Harness turn-run recipe injects the Bot ID
     into both the main and summarization sessions.
   - The Host patch build verifies each prepared reliability file against its
     protected manifest before it creates an image; the executor repair updates
     both the generated file and its manifest hash. The prepared reliability
     manifest is rejected when any entry no longer matches its file.

3. Auto review: retry once on a malformed classification and log failures
   (host/runtime/host-auto-review.mjs).

4. Web and image tools
   - Native web tools fall back to automatic tool choice when a model rejects a
     forced tool call; parallel searches succeed when one call succeeds
     (host/runtime/web-services.mjs).
   - Aspect ratios are mapped to image sizes, and reference images use the
     image edits endpoint (host/server/media-providers.mjs, media-http.mjs,
     media-settings.mjs, host/runtime/media-services.mjs).

5. Message order: messages from one model response are delivered in the order
   the model wrote them (host/runtime/reliability/tool-order.mjs (new),
   tool-journal.mjs, host/runtime/model-common.mjs). The reliability recipes
   for the tool-stream executor and Harness turn-run shell contain the guarded
   failure and Bot-ID changes described above.
   Subsequent model steps that immediately repeat an acknowledged single
   plain-text delivery stop before another send, without changing history
   (the three adapters, model-common.mjs and model-errors.mjs).

6. Linux deployment: host/release/build-docker.py accepts the image identity
   reported by Docker 29's containerd image store; host/network/build-tailcat.py
   builds the Windows target; Dockerfile.base and Dockerfile.execution set the
   executable bit on the Tailcat binary.

7. Admin command-line tool (new): host/tools/host-admin.mjs.

8. Tests: host/tests/ (new), windows/tests/ (new),
   mac/tests/desktop-external-links.test.mjs (locale-independent assertion).

9. Documentation: README, docs/AI-INSTALL, docs/ARCHITECTURE (now also covering
   the upstream DETAILS.md, TODO.md and install notes), module READMEs (host and
   ios now also cover the upstream DEPLOYMENT, PLUGINS and SIGNING notes),
   AGENTS.md, CHANGELOG, CONTRIBUTING, SECURITY, GitHub issue and pull request
   templates. The unused file list host/source-files.json was removed.

10. Android client (new)
   - android/shell/: Android shell app (Kotlin, no third-party libraries):
     loopback gateway to the paired Host, Keystore-encrypted credential,
     pairing, background notifications, file picking and saving, back gesture.
     android/dist/grokbot-android-shell.apk is its prebuilt release build.
   - android/client/: bridge that runs the original desktop interface in the
     Android WebView in place of Electron's main process and preloads, the
     computer view frame, a phone layout after the official phone app (the
     Bot list and conversations as separate screens, round floating buttons,
     message bubbles, full-screen pages and bottom sheets), an anchor
     positioning fallback and the connection page.
   - android/patchers/: builds the APK from the user's own official Windows
     installer (ZIP writing, APK Signature Scheme v2 signing with a key created
     for the user) and applies a few verified changes to the original
     interface (renderer-patches.mjs).
   - In 1.3.0, the interface comes from the Windows 1.1.0 installer by
     default, with 0.71.2 as a fallback (supported.json, renderer-patches.mjs
     per release). The bridge adds 1.1.0 dictation and startup defaults, a
     fresh computer view ticket on each load (gateway.js, webview.js),
     insertCSS for the VNC page, a moveBefore fallback (compat.js) and phone
     layouts for the 1.1.0 dialogs (android.css).
   - windows/patchers/desktop/original.mjs: extraction of the official
     installer moved out of patch.mjs so the Android patcher can share it.
   - android/tests/ (new).

11. Client reliability and validation: installer ownership checks, verified
    Windows installer inputs and cleanup, Android gateway limits, attachment
    save and notification fixes, distinct mobile and Windows device labels,
    model redirect protection and reliable ordered-message timeouts. Added
    regression tests, an optional cross-platform CI template and Android
    emulator screenshots, including real Chinese and English conversations.

12. ARM64 Host build path, locked ARM runtime dependencies, ARM64 Tailcat,
    deployment platform checks, operator CLI and upgrade safeguards; revised
    bilingual installation and architecture guides, version-input checks and
    deployment regression coverage. Documented Oracle Ampere A1 runtime
    verification with a separate amd64 desktop. The original desktop is unchanged.

13. Release engineering and reliability: streamed, fully verified Host patch
    output; public client-channel and cross-recipe checks; whole-guest resource
    observation; exact-image recovery on new volumes; model stream and device
    persistence fixes; desktop/mobile reconnect, attachment and pairing fixes;
    owned-file Windows installation and side-by-side legacy migration; admin
    UI/CLI failure handling and regression coverage. No upstream client or
    hosted runtime is distributed and this work does not change the license.

14. Revised the bilingual documentation shared by the platform archives:
    described managed-volume recovery, operator coordination across Docker
    daemons, and the remote execution node required in split Host mode.
    Distinguished historical upstream/A1 checks, failed candidate diagnostics
    and fresh-build timings from capacity or newer-client compatibility claims.

    Recovery distinguishes managed Host volumes from unrelated Compose names
    and project locks. Benchmark evidence binds running generations to start
    events and requires measurements inside the build phase.

15. Fixed two first-use behaviors. Windows client startup could overwrite a
    legacy Start menu shortcut and URL handler even after side-by-side install;
    occupied entries are preserved, and side-by-side and isolated QA launches
    register neither. With only a model configured on a split Host, the console
    waited indefinitely and the CLI timed out after three minutes. The console
    now opens the execution-node settings and the CLI reports saved, not applied.

16. Bounded HTTP error-body reads for all three model adapters. Oversized
    provider diagnostics are explicitly reported and canceled without losing
    the HTTP status or retry delay. Normal model responses are unaffected.

17. Validate the effective Compose mounts before switching services. Data
    directories must use the exact managed volume root, not a subdirectory;
    live inventory checks this before backup, too. Reject untracked or
    shadowing mounts before activation rather than after data has been opened.
    Warn before stopping the original Host when an unknown offline copy would
    preclude automatic recovery; retain the offline snapshot recovery path.

18. Release acceptance checks Android chat history and UI order after
    reconnect, distinguishes whole-guest capacity from Host diagnostics,
    and checks nested ZIP/APK and gzip content before distribution.
    The portable iOS CLI regressions use explicit UTF-8 subprocess output.

Client tools update (2026-11-14): separate Android app and renderer versions,
verify patched inputs in scratch, and publish independently checked client
tool archives. Official programs and generated clients are not distributed.
The server implementation is unchanged from the prior default branch.

ProkBot Plus 1.2.0 (2026-11-16): the Windows patcher accepts the official
Windows 1.1.0 installer (item 1), and the Host deployment, recovery, model
adapter and admin changes in items 13 to 18 are released. The Windows
installer acceptance workflow is an inactive template under ci/. Official
programs and generated clients are not distributed.

ProkBot Plus 1.2.1 (2026-11-16): android/client/compat.js adds built-in
functions missing from older Android System WebView builds before the
interface and the pairing page run, and explains a page that did not start
instead of leaving it blank.

ProkBot Plus 1.3.0 (2026-11-16): Windows and Android default to the official
1.1.0 interface and fall back to 0.71.2 (items 1 and 10). The Host is
unchanged. Official programs and generated clients are not distributed.

ProkBot Plus 1.3.1 (2026-11-17): host/release/backup.py reads the Docker
inspect keys that the daemon may omit (HostConfig.Mounts, VolumeOptions,
Subpath) with index, so backup and update work on Docker 29 with Compose 2.40
(item 17). Updated host/server/package-lock.json (hono, @hono/node-server,
body-parser) and the bundled mac/patchers/desktop/node_modules (@electron/asar
4.3.2 with glob and minimatch).

Tool-call validation (2026-11-15):
`host/runtime/openai-chat.mjs` and `host/runtime/openai-responses.mjs` omit
malformed historical function calls and their outputs during replay, and reject
malformed new function calls before they are persisted. This prevents a
provider's invalid function name from repeatedly breaking later turns.

